{
  "name": "Magnetic Pillar",
  "type": "spell",
  "img": "modules/titan-vttrpg-compendium/icons/traditions/Metal_Tradition_Icon.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": "<p>You summon a pillar of magnetic black iron that draws all other metal to it.</p><p>Choose an empty space within <strong>10 spaces</strong>. The pillar appears in that space until the start of your next turn.</p><p>When you cast this spell, all creatures within a <strong>5-space-radius</strong> of the pillar who are wielding metal weapons or wearing metal armor must make an opposed <strong>Resilience</strong> check.</p><p>On failure, any held metal weapons and objects are pulled from the wielder’s hands, sticking to the pillar.</p><p>If a creature wearing metal armor fails this check, they are forcibly pulled to the pillar, where they are <strong>Restrained</strong>.</p><p>A <strong>Restrained</strong> creature can use an <strong>Action</strong> to make a DN <strong>4:(1 + ES) Body (Athletics)</strong> check to free themselves, where <strong>ES</strong> is the number of extra successes on your casting check.</p><p>A non-restrained creature can use an <strong>Action</strong> to make the same check in order to free a weapon, creature or object that is stuck to the pillar.</p><p>Each extra success extends the duration by <strong>+1 rounds</strong>.</p><p><strong>Effect:</strong> @UUID[Compendium.titan-vttrpg-compendium.effects.ActiveEffect.PPwkqMc3V1cmynS5]{Magnetic Pillar}</p>",
